//==
// # Loop run witnesses (complexity sweep, chunk L2)
//
// A model's refinement loop run once per sweep, for the laws of layer 8 that read the loop's
// states and the mesh it assembles (pipeline.laws.plato: the step, refinement, watertightness and
// mesh-against-model laws). The law runner builds every Witness_* of these types once, before any
// law runs, and exhausts the finite list: neither type is generatable, since both hold a
// BrepModel and PipelineStates.

// A model and every state its refinement loop passes through under the witness options, every
// face chosen, and the mesh the last state assembles, without validation.
// Invariant: States[0] is InitialState, States[i + 1] is Step of States[i] while States[i] is not
// terminal, the last state is FinalState, and Mesh is AssembledMesh of the last state: the mesh
// MeshModel gives (UnvalidatedMesh).
type LoopRunWitness
{
    Name: String;
    Model: BrepModel;
    States: Array<PipelineState>;
    Mesh: ModelMesh;
}

// A loop run whose model takes longer to mesh than a law's budget (2 s compiled), so no law over
// it meshes the model again: the laws that run the pipeline a second time (determinism,
// metamorphic relations, current outcomes) run over LoopRunWitness only.
type CostlyLoopRunWitness
{
    Run: LoopRunWitness;
}
